{"id":147,"flavor":[{"games":["Shield"],"text":"This Pokémon was long considered to be no more than a myth. The small lump on a Dratini’s forehead is actually a horn that’s still coming in."},{"games":["Sword"],"text":"Dratini dwells near bodies of rapidly flowing water, such as the plunge pools of waterfalls. As it grows, Dratini will shed its skin many times."},{"games":["Let’s Go, Eevee!","Let’s Go, Pikachu!"],"text":"Long thought to be a myth, this Pokémon’s existence was only recently confirmed by a fisherman who caught one."},{"games":["Ultra Moon"],"text":"It sheds its skin—almost on a daily basis—and grows larger. Its skin is soft just after it’s been shed."},{"games":["Ultra Sun"],"text":"It’s still weak, so it lurks on the floor of bodies of water, eating whatever food sinks down and living a quiet life."},{"games":["Moon"],"text":"After a 10-hour struggle, a fisherman was able to pull one up and confirm its existence."},{"games":["Sun"],"text":"It grows by molting repeatedly. Boots made from the tanned cast-off skin are a super luxury item."},{"games":["Alpha Sapphire","Omega Ruby","Sapphire","Ruby"],"text":"Dratini continually molts and sloughs off its old skin. It does so because the life energy within its body steadily builds to reach uncontrollable levels."},{"games":["Y","SoulSilver","Silver"],"text":"This Pokémon is full of life energy. It continually sheds its skin and grows steadily larger."},{"games":["X","White 2","Black 2","White","Black","Platinum","Pearl","Diamond"],"text":"It is called the “Mirage Pokémon” because so few have seen it. Its shed skin has been found."},{"games":["HeartGold","Gold"],"text":"It is born large to start with. It repeatedly sheds its skin as it steadily grows longer."},{"games":["LeafGreen","Blue","Red"],"text":"Long considered a mythical POKéMON until recently, when a small colony was found living underwater."},{"games":["FireRed"],"text":"Even the young can exceed 6.5 feet in length. It grows larger by repeatedly shedding skin."},{"games":["Emerald"],"text":"A DRATINI continually molts and sloughs off its old skin. It does so because the life energy within its body steadily builds to reach uncontrollable levels."}],"abilities":[{"name":"Shed Skin","hidden":false,"description":"The Pokémon may cure its own status conditions by shedding its skin."},{"name":"Marvel Scale","hidden":true,"description":"The Pokémon's marvelous scales boost its Defense stat if it has a status condition."}],"eggGroups":["Water 1","Dragon"],"genderRate":4,"hatchCounter":40,"baseHappiness":35,"growthRate":"slow","habitat":"water's edge","color":"Blue","shape":"Squiggle","evolution":{"id":147,"name":"Dratini","condition":null,"children":[{"id":148,"name":"Dragonair","condition":"Lv. 30","children":[{"id":149,"name":"Dragonite","condition":"Lv. 55","children":[]}]}]},"moves":{"game":"Scarlet / Violet","level":[[1,35],[1,43],[5,239],[10,86],[15,525],[20,97],[25,21],[31,401],[35,407],[40,219],[45,240],[50,349],[55,200],[60,63]],"machine":[97,59,34,784,886,434,913,349,406,525,203,263,126,83,53,416,114,270,56,63,58,196,442,113,200,182,240,156,799,214,164,241,57,129,36,851,87,86,85,352,127],"egg":[453,225,245,54,48,352],"tutor":[]},"cards":[{"id":"me2pt5-150","name":"Dratini","set":"Ascended Heroes","date":"2026-01-30","rarity":"Common","number":"150","artist":"HYOGONOSUKE","small":"https://images.scrydex.com/pokemon/me2pt5-150/small","large":"https://images.scrydex.com/pokemon/me2pt5-150/large"},{"id":"sv3pt5-147","name":"Dratini","set":"151","date":"2023-09-22","rarity":"Common","number":"147","artist":"Sanosuke Sakuma","img":"sv3pt5/147"},{"id":"sv3-157","name":"Dratini","set":"Obsidian Flames","date":"2023-08-11","rarity":"Common","number":"157","artist":"satoma","img":"sv3/157"},{"id":"swsh12-129","name":"Dratini","set":"Silver Tempest","date":"2022-11-11","rarity":"Common","number":"129","artist":"kurumitsu","img":"swsh12/129"},{"id":"sm11-147","name":"Dratini","set":"Unified Minds","date":"2019-08-02",